.patch","merged_at":"2026-02-20T02:31:49Z"},"body":"Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114843\r\n\r\nThis PR proposes a partially alternative solution to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114843, that (I believe) is a bit more intuitive.\r\n\r\nThis PR adds 3 new methods: `Input.is_joy_vibrating()`, `Input.has_joy_vibration()` and `Input.get_joy_vibration_remaining_duration()`. Note that currently the only platforms that support joypad vibration are the desktop platforms and (probably?) iOS (which should also move to SDL joypad implementation and `JoypadFeatures` usage in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114316). I'm not sure Android vibration is viable, see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114347, and web vibration will be implemented in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114344.\r\n\r\nThis PR also documents the behaviour of `Input.get_joy_vibration_strength()` and `Input.get_joy_vibration_duration()` noticed in the linked issue.\r\n\r\nI haven't tested this PR yet though, because I temporarily don't have access to my DualShock 4 😅(EDIT: Now I tested it and it seems to work for me)\r\n\r\nTODO:\r\n- [x] `is_joy_vibrating()` incorrectly calculates the finishing timestamp, since the timestamp is in usec, not msec\r\n- [x] `get_joy_vibration_remaining_duration()`\r\n- [x] Don't use bitfield for joypad class","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organization